## 16. How to prepare for L2/L3 interviews in 30 days

## Days 1–7

Linux core and storage

Revise advanced commands, permissions, systemd, boot recovery, LVM, filesystems and disk troubleshooting. Perform the exercises on a test VM.

## Days 8–14

Networking and performance

Practice DNS failures, TCP connections, firewalld, high load, memory pressure, packet captures and service troubleshooting.

## Days 15–21

Production applications and hosting

Revise Apache/Nginx, PHP-FPM, TLS, cPanel/WHM, Plesk, MySQL replication, email troubleshooting and ELK.

## Days 22–30

L3 scenarios and mock interviews

Practice root-cause analysis, Bash/Ansible automation, AWS recovery, disaster recovery, incident reports and architecture discussions.

My recommendation is to prioritize Linux troubleshooting, networking, storage, performance, Apache/Nginx, MySQL and hosting incidents first. Then strengthen automation, AWS and advanced architecture to demonstrate L3-level skills.

Interview tip: For each scenario, explain the symptoms, commands you would run, how you interpret the output, the root cause, the recovery steps and the preventive action. Avoid jumping straight to restarting a service or rebooting a production server.

